When the runtime power management level is zero, both the device power mode and link state remain active. In that case, the condition is true, causing the code to jump directly to `vops_suspend` without executing the `flush_work(&hba->eeh_work)` that appears later in the function. This leaves a pending exception event handling work item that can subsequently try to access the host controller hardware after the system has entered a deep power‑down state, resulting in an illegal access and a system crash.

