```c
ufshcd_disable_auto_bkops(hba);
flush_work(&hba->eeh_work);
```
Reason:
By explicitly disabling auto bkops and flushing the exception event handling work (`eeh_work`) before the early `goto vops_suspend`, the fix ensures that any pending exception tasks are completed and that no new auto bkops are started during the critical window. This prevents the illegal hardware access after the system enters a deep power‑down state, eliminating the race condition.

